TESTSUITE "flow-target mocks"

*> Mocking a paragraph/section replaces its whole body for this case --
*> including the CALL inside CALC-TOTALS, which therefore needs no
*> MOCK CALL of its own here.
TESTCASE "mocked paragraph and section replace their bodies"
    MOCK PARAGRAPH CALC-TOTALS
        MOVE 42 TO WS-TOTAL
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SECTION RPT-BLOCK
        ADD 7 TO WS-TOTAL
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM MAIN-PROCESS
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL TO BE 50
    VERIFY PARAGRAPH CALC-TOTALS WAS PERFORMED ONCE
    VERIFY SECTION RPT-BLOCK WAS PERFORMED ONCE

*> With no flow mocks, the real bodies run -- so the CALL boundary must
*> be mocked, exactly as before this feature existed.
TESTCASE "real bodies run when not mocked"
    MOCK CALL "RATECALC"
        MOVE 0 TO WS-RC
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM MAIN-PROCESS
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL TO BE 306

TESTCASE "mocked section only, real paragraph"
    MOCK CALL "RATECALC"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SECTION RPT-BLOCK
        ADD 7 TO WS-TOTAL
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM MAIN-PROCESS
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL TO BE 13
    VERIFY SECTION RPT-BLOCK WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY CALL "RATECALC" WAS CALLED ONCE
